comments.body:
[claude] Done. PR #113 merged (claude author; approved by devin and antigravity after the last commit, CI green).

Acceptance ("a test where the agent writes a profile file and a PATH shim that would fake `git` / `python3`, and the host check's verdict does not change; the agent's own commands keep the login shell"): `backend/tests/test_sandbox_verification.py`, run in the real `anvil-sandbox-rtems:7.1` image as the real `agent` user (skipped without Docker or the image), each test showing the attack on the agent's own shell first (the control):

* a planted PATH shim plus a profile line: the agent's shell prints FAKE and HIJACKED; `run_verified` prints 42 and neither;
* a planted `core.fsmonitor` in the repo's `.git/config` runs under the agent's `git status` and does not run under `run_verified`;
* check scripts uploaded with `upload_trusted` are `root 644` in a `root 755` directory; the agent's append fails; the hardened runner still executes them;
* argv-level tests: no login shell and a clean environment for verification (`env -i`, `bash --noprofile --norc`, no outer shell); `execute` and `run_internal` still use `bash -lc`.
`verify_outcome` also fails closed now (a failed git command is a failed verification, not "nothing changed") and uses the open PR whose head is the run's last commit (P1-15): `test_a_failed_git_command_is_a_failed_verification_not_nothing_changed`, `test_a_pr_that_does_not_contain_the_runs_last_commit_is_flagged`, `test_the_open_pr_with_the_runs_head_decides_not_a_stale_closed_one`. Offline chain test 2/2 through the hardened path.

Not covered (known limits): an agent that leaves a background process running can still race a check by changing repository files while it runs (the real defence is verifying from host-captured hashes, ANVIL-100); the setup commands (checkout, export, push) still use the login shell on purpose; the RTEMS toolchain is not on the verification PATH (the python3/git checks don't need it).
